{"level":30,"time":1794927832843,"pid":16195,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"9f667f00-9b95-4b74-ac94-27f6c19ca906","event":"model_request","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties. Initial research plan: {\"understand\":[\"La question porte sur la fonction activate() dans extension.ts, spécifiquement les lignes 81 à 114.\",\"Objectif : identifier quelles fonctionnalités CodeTour y sont initialisées (commandes, providers, listeners, état initial).\",\"La réponse doit être un JSON concis avec citations directes du code et un champ d'incertitudes explicites.\",\"Le catalogue fourni est vide : aucune fonction de réutilisation connue a priori.\"],\"investigate\":[\"Localiser extension.ts à la racine du dépôt codetour (probablement ./src/extension.ts ou ./extension.ts) et lire les lignes 81 à 114.\",\"Extraire chaque appel d'initialisation dans activate() : registerCommand, registerXxxProvider, registerTextDocumentContentProvider, workspace.onDidChangeWorkspaceFolders, window.registerWebviewPanelSerializer, etc.\",\"Vérifier si activate() charge un état persistant (ex. tour courant via workspaceState ou un fichier .tour) et si registerContentProvider('codetour', ...) est présent.\",\"Noter les conditions d'activation (activationEvents dans package.json) pour contextualiser, sans sortir du périmètre des lignes 81-114.\",\"Citer chaque ligne pertinente verbatim avec son numéro, puis lister les incertitudes : dépendances importées non visibles dans l'extrait, ordre d'initialisation, effets de bord différés (promesses non attendues).\"],\"reuse\":[]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: []. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. When a reusable procedure would add value and no stored procedure or primitive already covers it, try function_try to compose primitives into structured, cited evidence. Do not create a function merely to satisfy a quota; conclud