{"level":30,"time":1794928177732,"pid":25299,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"eeadd765-8133-42bb-95ed-1ad3dbb26f8b","event":"model_response","response":{"result":{"candidate":{"name":"summarizeModuleEntryFromLines","question":"Que fait la fonction d'entrée <entryPoint> dans <file>, en citant uniquement les lignes <startLine> à <endLine>, et quels appels/imports y sont reliés (sans explorer leur détail) ?","description":"Reads an exact line range of one file and produces a structured summary of a module entry point: the verbatim cited lines, the imported symbols declared in that range, the zero-argument calls made inside the declared function(s), and the relations entry-point -> callee backed by line evidence. Optionally, for each callee imported from a relative module, it runs one symbol search to record where the symbol is defined (file and line only, contents are not read), so relations are not purely assumed. Output: { file, range, citedLines, imports, entryPoints, relations, definitionLocations, uncertainties }. Limits: only the requested line range is read; bodies of imported modules are never opened (definition lookup returns locations only); parsing is regex-based on simple 'import { x } from \"./y\"' and 'name()' statements, so exotic syntax may be missed and is reported as an uncertainty.","source":"async ({ readLines, search }: { readLines: (p: { file: string; startLine: number; endLine: number }) => Promise<{ result: { lines: { line: number; text: string }[] } }>; search: (p: { query: string }) => Promise<{ result: { matches: { file: string; line: number; text: string }[] } }> }) => async (params: { file: string; startLine: number; endLine: number; entryPoint?: string; locateDefinitions?: boolean }): Promise<{ file: string; range: { startLine: number; endLine: number }; citedLines: { line: number; text: string }[]; imports: { name: string; module: string; line: number }[]; entryPoints: { name: string; evidence: { file: string; startLine: number; endLine: number } }[]; relations: { from: string; to: string; evidence: { file: string; startLine: number; endLine: number } }[]; definitionLocations: { name: string; file: string; line: number }[]; uncertainties: string[] }> => {\n  const { file, startLine, endLine, entryPoint, locateDefinitions = false } = params;\n  const uncertainties: string[] = [];\n  const read = await readLines({ file, startLine, endLine });\n  const lines = read.result.lines;\n  if (lines.length === 0) {\n    return { file, range: { startLine, endLine }, citedLines: [], imports: [], entryPoints: [], relations: [], definitionLocations: [], uncertainties: [\"No lines returned for the requested range; nothing was analyzed.\"] };\n  }\n  const citedLines = lines.map((l) => ({ line: l.line, text: l.text }));\n  const imports: { name: string; module: string; line: number }[] = [];\n  const importRe = /import\\s+\\{\\s*([A-Za-z_$][\\w$]*)\\s*\\}\\s+from\\s+[\"']([^\"']+)[\"']/;\n  for (const l of lines) {\n    const m = importRe.exec(l.text);\n    if (m) imports.push({ name: m[1], module: m[2], line: l.line });\n  }\n  const fnRe = /(?:export\\s+)?(?:async\\s+)?function\\s+([A-Za-z_$][\\w$]*)/;\n  const declared: { name: string; startLine: number; endLine: number }[] = [];\n  for (const l of lines) {\n    const m = fnRe.exec(l.text);\n    if (m) declared.push({ name: m[1], startLine: l.line, endLine: l.line });\n  }\n  for (const d of declared) {\n    const open = lines.find((l) => l.line >= d.startLine && l.text.includes(\"{\"));\n    const close = [...lines].reverse().find((l) => l.line >= d.startLine && l.text.includes(\"}\"));\n    if (open) d.startLine = open.line;\n    if (close) d.endLine = close.line;\n  }\n  const entryPoints = (entryPoint ? declared.filter((d) => d.name === entryPoint) : declared).map((d) => ({ name: d.name, evidence: { file, startLine: d.startLine, endLine: d.endLine } }));\n  if (entryPoint && entryPoints.length === 0) uncertainties.push(`Entry point \"${entryPoint}\" was not found as a function declaration within lines ${startLine}-${endLine} of ${file}.`);\n  const importByName = new Map(imports.map((i) => [i.name, i]));\n  const relations: { from: string; to: string; evidence: { file: string; startLine: number; endLine: number } }[] = [];\n  for (const ep of entryPoints) {\n    const body = lines.filter((l) => l.line >= ep.evidence.startLine && l.line <= ep.evidence.endLine);\n    const callRe = /([A-Za-z_$][\\w$]*)\\s*\\(/g;\n    for (const l of body) {\n      let m: RegExpExecArray | null;\n      while ((m = callRe.exec(l.text)) !== null) {\n        const callee = m[1];\n        if (callee === ep.name || callee === \"function\") continue;\n        if (importByName.has(callee)) {\n          if (!relations.some((r) => r.from === ep.name && r.to === callee)) {\n            relations.push({ from: ep.name, to: callee, evidence: { file, startLine: l.line, endLine: l.line } });\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  const definitionLocations: { name: string; file: string; line: number }[] = [];\n  if (locateDefinitions) {\n    for (const r of relations) {\n      try {\n        const hit = await search({ query: `export function ${r.to}` });\n        const first = hit.result.matches.find((x) => x.file !== file);\n        if (first) definitionLocations.push({ name: r.to, file: first.file, line: first.line });\n        else uncertainties.push(`No definition location found for \"${r.to}\"; relation is based on the import and call site only.`);\n      } catch {\n        uncertainties.push(`Definition lookup for \"${r.to}\" failed; relation is based on the import and call site only.`);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  uncertainties.push(`Only lines ${startLine} to ${endLine} of ${file} were read; the rest of the file was not examined.`);\n  if (relations.length > 0) uncertainties.push(\"The internal details of the called/imported modules (e.g. registered commands or providers) were not explored.\");\n  uncertainties.push(\"Parsing is regex-based on simple import and call statements; syntactic matches are evidence, not semantic certainty.\");\n  return { file, range: { startLine, endLine }, citedLines, imports, entryPoints, relations, definitionLocations, uncertainties };\n}","params":{"file":"recorder/index.ts","startLine":1,"endLine":7,"entryPoint":"registerRecorderModule","locateDefinitions":false}}},"usage":{"inputTokens":719,"outputTokens":2540}},"model":{"model":"zai-glm-5-3-flash","temperature":0,"maxOutputTokens":16384}}
