{"level":30,"time":1794928217097,"pid":26585,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"b15f4196-2640-4e69-9482-98db8f37b66f","event":"model_request","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"Investigate the supplied technical question. Treat the initial research plan as a flexible guide: follow new evidence freely without revising or tracking the plan. When memory is enabled, consult memory_list for useful capabilities and run matching procedures with memory_run, verify their evidence, and investigate only what is missing. In Code Mode with memory, use function_try to explore via the provided primitives and propose useful parameterized procedures. Do not recreate equivalent procedures or nest memorized procedures. Do not write a Tour. Return sourced findings and explicit uncertainties. Initial research plan: {\"understand\":[\"La question porte sur le mécanisme d'enregistrement du serveur MCP fourni par CodeTour, spécifiquement pour les dossiers ouverts dans VS Code.\",\"Deux fichiers sont explicitement visés : desktopIntegration.ts et mcp.ts. Il faut lire les deux et citer les lignes pertinentes.\",\"Il faut identifier les conditions d'enregistrement (ex. : type d'hôte, présence d'un workspace/dossier ouvert, activation de l'extension, version de VS Code, feature flag).\",\"Le catalogue est vide : aucune fonction réutilisable n'est disponible, l'investigation reposera donc sur la lecture directe des fichiers et de leurs imports/références.\"],\"investigate\":[\"Localiser desktopIntegration.ts et mcp.ts dans le dépôt (recherche de fichiers par nom) et lire chacun en entier pour comprendre leur rôle et leurs exports.\",\"Dans mcp.ts, identifier la classe/fonction qui implémente ou expose le serveur MCP (outils fournis par CodeTour) et repérer les lignes où le serveur est créé, configuré ou démarré.\",\"Dans desktopIntegration.ts, repérer le point d'entrée qui déclenche l'enregistrement du serveur MCP (appel à mcp.ts ou à une API d'extension VS Code) et noter les numéros de lignes exactes.\",\"Extraire les conditions d'enregistrement : vérifier les gardes (if/guard clauses) autour de l'appel — par exemple vérification qu'un workspace/dossier est ouvert (vscode.workspace.workspaceFolders), contexte d'exécution, mode desktop vs web, ou option de configuration.\",\"Tracer les imports entre les deux fichiers et chercher d'autres références à mcp.ts (ex. dans extension.ts ou package.json contributes) pour confirmer que desktopIntegration.ts est bien le seul chemin d'enregistrement pour les dossiers ouverts.\",\"Vérifier le comportement en l'absence de dossier ouvert (workspace vide ou fichiers isolés) pour décrire précisément quand l'enregistrement ne se produit pas.\",\"Rédiger la réponse avec : extraits de code cités (fichier + numéros de lignes) pour chaque étape d'enregistrement, et liste explicite des conditions nécessaires et suffisantes.\"],\"reuse\":[]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: []. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. When a reusable procedure would add value and no stored procedure or primitive already covers it, try function_try to compose primitives into structured, cited evidence. Do not create a function merely to satisfy a quota; conclude when the evidence is sufficient. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable. The catalogue above is already complete: do not call memory_list to rediscover it. If no entry fits, build the missing procedure with function_try early instead of repeating searches."},{"role":"user","content":"Comment desktopIntegration.ts et mcp.ts enregistrent-ils le serveur MCP fourni par CodeTour pour les dossiers ouverts ? Lis ces deux fichiers, cite les lignes utiles et indique les conditions."},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b710e94c8257554","type":"function","function":{"name":"listFiles","arguments":"{}"}},{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f251d251bd590a2","type":"function","function":{"name":"searchText","arguments":"{\"query\":\"mcp\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b710e94c8257554","content":"{\"result\":[\".DS_Store\",\".tours/.memory/b6f7ac2cdf7e9cfd6f12eaffefc3ebd7676d1e8405d5890db286e7a71df9299e.json\",\".tours/.memory/functions/findSymbolOccurrences.ts\",\".tours/config.json\",\"agent/acpAgentProcess.ts\",\"agent/acpProviders.test.ts\",\"agent/acpProviders.ts\",\"agent/acpSession.test.ts\",\"agent/acpSession.ts\",\"agent/fakeAcpAgent.ts\",\"agent/fallbackStepChatAgent.ts\",\"agent/stepChatAgent.ts\",\"agent/stepChatContract.ts\",\"agent/stepConversations.test.ts\",\"agent/stepConversations.ts\",\"agent/vibeAcpEntry.test.ts\",\"agent/vibeAcpEntry.ts\",\"api.ts\",\"cli/agentIntegrations.test.ts\",\"cli/agentIntegrations.ts\",\"cli/cli.test.ts\",\"cli/copilot-extension.generated.ts\",\"cli/html.test.ts\",\"cli/html.ts\",\"cli/index.ts\",\"cli/narration/NarrationController.test.ts