{"level":30,"time":1794928249731,"pid":27457,"hostname":"r179-30-55-14.dialup.mobile.ancel.net.uy","runId":"0ecd75e4-f1e4-41d0-b34e-fec662f41a65","event":"model_response","response":{"result":{"candidate":{"name":"extractFunctionSourceWithLineNumbers","question":"Comment la fonction « registerMcpProvider » dans mcp.ts définit-elle le serveur MCP pour chaque dossier ouvert, et quelles lignes exactes (avec numéros) en constituent le corps ?","description":"Reproduces the cited evidence for a single-function code-explanation question in one file. Given a file name and an exported function name, the procedure first locates the function's declaration line via a text search restricted to that file, then reads a bounded window of lines starting at that declaration, and finally trims the window to the function's closing brace (a line that is exactly '}'). Output is the ordered list of {line, text} records covering the function body, suitable as line-cited evidence. Limits: assumes the function is declared at top level with 'function <name>' and closed by a brace-only line; it does not analyze semantics, does not follow calls into other files, and returns an empty result if the declaration is not found or the body exceeds maxLines.","source":"async ({ file, functionName, maxLines = 200 }: { file: string; functionName: string; maxLines?: number }) => {\n  const decl = await searchText({ query: `function ${functionName}`, file });\n  const hit = decl.result.find(r => r.file === file && new RegExp(`(export\\\\s+)?(async\\\\s+)?function\\\\s+${functionName}\\\\b`).test(r.text));\n  if (!hit) return { file, functionName, lines: [] };\n  const startLine = hit.line;\n  const window = await readLines({ file, startLine, endLine: startLine + maxLines - 1 });\n  const lines = window.result.lines;\n  const endIdx = lines.findIndex(l => l.text.trim() === \"}\");\n  const body = endIdx === -1 ? lines : lines.slice(0, endIdx + 1);\n  return { file, functionName, startLine, lines: body };\n