 donc si 'activate' apparaît dans de nombreux fichiers, la déclaration dans extension.ts pourrait ne pas figurer dans les 20 premiers résultats ; en cas d'échec, relancer avec une limite plus élevée ou affiner la recherche.\"],\"reuse\":[\"searchIdentifiers\",\"searchText\"]}\n\nExplore the repository using the tools. Assess whether the evidence answers the objective; if essential evidence is missing, use further tools before returning. Record unresolved gaps in uncertainties. Return only JSON matching this exact shape: {\"objective\":\"...\",\"entryPoints\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"components\":[{\"name\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"relations\":[{\"from\":\"...\",\"to\":\"...\",\"evidence\":[{\"file\":\"relative/path\",\"startLine\":1,\"endLine\":1}]}],\"uncertainties\":[\"...\"]}. Use empty arrays when needed. Each evidence must be an array of objects with real file paths and integer line numbers, not a string. Copy line numbers exactly from tool output (each numbered line, match or range); never estimate, recompute or round them. Do not write a tour. Script memory is enabled. memory_list(query) returns the catalogue WITHOUT function source code: id (TypeScript identifier), objective (canonical question), description (scope), typed params, output contract, limits and uncertainty cases. Available entries: []. If a listed function can help, call memory_run with its id and suitable params, verify its proofs, and complete only what is missing. The permanent primitives (listFiles, searchText, searchIdentifiers, readLines, readLineFragment, readAround, listSymbols, findDefinitions, findReferences, getImports, getGitDiff) are available as direct tools: use them for simple reads and searches. When a reusable procedure would add value and no stored procedure or primitive already covers it, try function_try to compose primitives into structured, cited evidence. Do not create a function merely to satisfy a quota; conclude when the evidence is sufficient. Use a TypeScript function expression with typed inputs; the harness passes params to it. searchText(query) returns {file,line,text}[], readLines(file,start,end) returns {file,start,lines,nextLine,truncatedLines}; continue with nextLine and the same end, and recover truncated lines with readLineFragment(file,line,offset), starting at offset 0 and continuing with nextOffset. listFiles() returns paths. Give useful procedures a valid TypeScript identifier and parameterize variations. When a stored procedure fails or is unusable for its declared subject, you may submit a corrected function_try under its existing id only if its purpose and contract remain unchanged; otherwise use a new name. Supply question as a stable canonical question independent of this Tour and a non-empty English description (ASCII only: no accented characters, even when the question is in French) stating what the procedure does, its scope, the shape of its result and its key limits. Every successfully executed function_try trial is automatically submitted to post-Tour selection — no remember flag is needed; the selection step considers actual contribution, correctness, documentation and duplication, and consolidation re-executes the exact code and params and re-checks every citation, so only deterministically validated selections persist. Do not wrap a primitive merely to remember it. Combine independent outputs in your Tour logic; never call one memorized procedure from another. Syntactic matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations; report missing evidence as uncertainty. If a stored function was selected for its declared subject but returned unusable output, call memory_unusable. The catalogue above is already complete: do not call memory_list to rediscover it. If no entry fits, build the missing procedure with function_try early instead of repeating searches."},{"role":"user","content":"Où activate est-elle déclarée dans extension.ts ? Essaie tôt cette fonction paramétrable avec {\"symbol\":\"activate\",\"limit\":20} pour localiser des références, puis réponds avec la ligne pertinente et les limites :\n(params: {symbol: string, limit?: number}) => {\n  const limit = params.limit ?? 3;\n  const byId = searchIdentifiers(params.symbol).map(r => ({file: r.file, line: r.line, text: r.text || ''}));\n  const byText = searchText(params.symbol).map(r => ({file: r.file, line: r.line, text: r.text || ''}));\n  const seen = new Set<string>();\n  const out: {file: string, line: number, text: string}[] = [];\n  for (const r of [...byId, ...byText]) {\n    const key = r.file + ':' + r.line;\n    if (seen.has(key)) continue;\n    seen.add(key);\n    out.push(r);\n    if (out.length >= limit) break;\n  }\n  return out;\n}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b97675475246bb04","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"description\":\"Locates occurrences of a symbol by combining searchIdentifiers and searchText, deduplicating by file:line and returning up to limit results. Scope: whole repository, syntactic matches only. Result shape: array of {file, line, text}. Limits: at most limit results after dedup, so the declaration may be missed if the symbol is frequent; matches are candidates, not proven semantic relations.\",\"name\":\"findSymbolOccurrences\",\"params\":{\"limit\":20,\"symbol\":\"activate\"},\"question\":\"Where is the function activate declared in extension.ts?\",\"source\":\"(params: {symbol: string, limit?: number}) => {\\n  const limit = params.limit ?? 3;\\n  const byId = searchIdentifiers(params.symbol).map(r => ({file: r.file, line: r.line, text: r.text || ''}));\\n  const byText = searchText(params.symbol).map(r => ({file: r.file, line: r.line, text: r.text || ''}));\\n  const seen = new Set<string>();\\n  const out: {file: string, line: number, text: string}[] = [];\\n  for (const r of [...byId, ...byText]) {\\n    const key = r.file + ':' + r.line;\\n    if (seen.has(key)) continue;\\n    seen.add(key);\\n    out.push(r);\\n    if (out.length >= limit) break;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b97675475246bb04","content":"{\"result\":[{\"file\":\".tours/architecture_extension_codetour.tour\",\"line\":12,\"text\":\"      \\\"description\\\": \\\"`activate` branche les intégrations de bureau, le lecteur et l’enregistreur, puis configure notamment la conversation sur les étapes. Quand des dossiers sont ouverts, l’extension lance la découverte des tours avant de poursuivre l’initialisation.\\\\n\\\\nLes fonctions appelées restent responsables de leurs propres détails ; les étapes suivantes examinent celles qui structurent ce parcours.\\\",\"},{\"file\":\".tours/architecture_extension_codetour.tour\",\"line\":14,\"text\":\"      \\\"pattern\\\": \\\"export async function activate\\\\\\\\(\\\"\"},{\"file\":\"extension.ts\",\"line\":81,\"text\":\"export async function activate(context: vscode.ExtensionContext) {\"},{\"file\":\"git.ts\",\"line\":43,\"text\":\"    await extension.activate();\"},{\"file\":\"player/codeStatus.ts\",\"line\":11,\"text\":\"    await extension.activate();\"}],\"returned\":5,\"observed\":5,\"truncated\":false,\"bounds\":{\"maxItems\":50,\"maxBytes\":8000},\"bytes\":900,\"revision\":\"3e8f2aa7da11dd6d26bbb6e3dffde679471c9780\",\"provenance\":\"primitive-derived\",\"uncertainty\":[\"Primitive matches provide syntactic evidence, not semantic certainty or proof of absence.\"],\"descriptionWarning\":\"Description is too long: 390 characters; at most 300 are allowed. Resubmit this function_try with a corrected ASCII-only English description or the trial will be refused at consolidation.\"}"},{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a1dcab9931dfdf33","type":"function","function":{"name":"function_try","arguments":"{\"description\":\"Locates occurrences of a symbol by combining searc